IMPORT prelude

-- Theft Act 1968 (1968 c. 60) -- THE NOUNS. Layer 1.
--
-- This module holds DECLAREs only: the enumerations and the fact records every
-- other module of the encoding reads. No rules, no assertions. A fact is
-- something a witness of ordinary competence could testify to ("he took it
-- with him", "he believed he had the owner's consent"); whether those facts
-- make an offence is a rule, and the rule lives in the module for its section.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1968-60.txt, a plain-text rendering (not the official
-- text) of the legislation.gov.uk revised version of 2013-05-28.
--
-- Naming. Every field name is distinct across all records in this encoding, and
-- no field name begins with "is" or "has": the genitive ('s) already supplies
-- the verb ("the facts' dishonest apart from ..." reads "the facts are ...").
-- Words of state of mind and judgment are fields that the person states; the
-- Act's own definitions are worked out by the rules from the other fields.

§ `Theft Act 1968 -- nouns`

§§ `Penalties`

-- How the Act says a penalty is reached.
DECLARE `Mode of conviction` IS ONE OF
    `on conviction on indictment`
    `on summary conviction`

-- The ceiling on imprisonment that the section itself states.
DECLARE `Imprisonment ceiling` IS ONE OF
    `imprisonment for life`
    `imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` HAS `years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of months` HAS `months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
    `the section states no imprisonment`

-- The ceiling on a fine that the section itself states. The Act gives a LEVEL on
-- the standard scale; the sum of money for a level is not in the text, so no
-- sum is carried here.
DECLARE `Fine ceiling` IS ONE OF
    `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` HAS `level on the standard scale` IS A NUMBER
    `the section states no fine`

-- A penalty exactly as the section states it. Nothing is imported from
-- sentencing law: where the section states no fine, the fine ceiling says so.
DECLARE `Penalty stated by the Act` HAS
    `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS AN `Imprisonment ceiling`
    `the fine ceiling` IS A `Fine ceiling`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What a section makes of a set of facts: no offence, an offence with the
-- penalty the section states, or an offence for which the text states no penalty.
DECLARE `Outcome of a charge` IS ONE OF
    `no offence under this section on these facts`
    `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` HAS `the penalty the section states` IS A `Penalty stated by the Act`
    `an offence, but the text states no penalty for it`

§§ `Sections 1 to 6 -- the definition of theft`

-- s 2. "Dishonestly".
DECLARE `Dishonesty facts` HAS
    `believed in law he had the right to deprive the other of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believed he would have the other's consent if the other knew` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believed the owner cannot be discovered by taking reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the property came to him as trustee or personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `willing to pay for the property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dishonest apart from the section 2(1) beliefs` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 3. "Appropriates".
DECLARE `Appropriation facts` HAS
    `assumed the rights of an owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `came by the property without stealing it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `later assumed a right to it by keeping or dealing with it as owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `property or an interest in it was transferred, or purported to be, to him for value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acted in good faith when it was transferred to him` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rights assumed are rights he believed himself to be acquiring` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the transferor's title` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4. "Property". The kind of thing taken, as a witness would describe it.
DECLARE `Kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `money`
    `a thing in action or other intangible property`
    `other personal property`
    `land itself`
    `a thing forming part of land`
    `mushrooms, or flowers, fruit or foliage, picked from a plant growing wild on land`
    `a wild creature that is tamed or ordinarily kept in captivity`
    `a wild creature that is neither tamed nor ordinarily kept in captivity, or the carcase of one`
    `something that is not property within section 4(1)`

DECLARE `Thing taken` HAS
    `kind of thing` IS A `Kind of thing`
    `in possession of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised as trustee, personal representative, attorney or otherwise to sell or dispose of land belonging to another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dealt with it in breach of the confidence reposed in him` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appropriated it by severing it, causing it to be severed, or after it had been severed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in possession of the land under a tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `remains in possession of the land after a tenancy ended, as statutory tenant or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a fixture or structure let to be used with the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `picked it for reward, or for sale or other commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has been reduced into possession by or on behalf of another person and possession has not since been lost or abandoned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another person is in course of reducing it into possession` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 5. "Belonging to another". Every field is about someone OTHER THAN the person
-- who appropriates.
DECLARE `Belonging facts` HAS
    `another had possession or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another had a proprietary right or interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every such interest of another is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was subject to a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another had a right to enforce the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he received it from or on account of another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he was under an obligation to that other to retain and deal with it or its proceeds in a particular way` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he got it by another's mistake` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he was under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of it, its proceeds or its value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is property of a corporation sole, the office being vacant or not` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other is the wife or husband of the person who appropriates it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other's interest in it is derived from the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 6. "With the intention of permanently depriving the other of it", with the
-- two intentions that s 5(2) and s 5(4) say are to be regarded as such.
DECLARE `Intention facts` HAS
    `meant the other permanently to lose the thing itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meant to treat the thing as his own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the way he meant to treat it was a borrowing or lending` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the borrowing or lending was for a period and in circumstances making it equivalent to an outright taking or disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had possession or control of the property, lawfully or not` IS A BOOLEAN
    `parted with the property under a condition as to its return which he may not be able to perform` IS A BOOLEAN
    `parted with it for purposes of his own` IS A BOOLEAN
    `parted with it without the other's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meant to defeat the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meant not to make restoration` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 1. One act of appropriation, with the five matters ss 2 to 6 define.
DECLARE `Theft facts` HAS
    `the dishonesty` IS A `Dishonesty facts`
    `the appropriation` IS AN `Appropriation facts`
    `the thing taken` IS A `Thing taken`
    `the belonging` IS A `Belonging facts`
    `the intention` IS AN `Intention facts`
    `with a view to gain or for his own benefit` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Sections 7 to 14 -- theft, robbery, burglary, etc.`

-- s 8.
DECLARE `Robbery facts` HAS
    `the stealing` IS A `Theft facts`
    `used force on any person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `put or sought to put any person in fear of being then and there subjected to force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately before or at the time of stealing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in order to steal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed an assault with intent to rob` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 9.
DECLARE `Burglary facts` HAS
    `the place entered is a building or part of a building` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the place entered is an inhabited vehicle or vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the place entered is a dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entered as a trespasser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at entry he intended to steal anything in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at entry he intended to inflict grievous bodily harm on a person in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at entry he intended to do unlawful damage to it or anything in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stealing after entry` IS A `Theft facts`
    `the property stolen was in the building or that part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `after entry he attempted to steal anything in the building or that part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `after entry he inflicted or attempted to inflict grievous bodily harm on a person in it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 10.
DECLARE `Aggravated burglary facts` HAS
    `the burglary` IS A `Burglary facts`
    `at the time had with him a firearm, including an airgun or air pistol` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the time had with him anything with the appearance of a firearm, whether or not capable of being discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the time had with him an article made or adapted for use for causing injury to or incapacitating a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the time had with him an article he intended for causing injury to or incapacitating a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the time had with him an article manufactured for the purpose of producing a practical effect by explosion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the time had with him an article he intended for the purpose of producing a practical effect by explosion` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 11.
DECLARE `Removal facts` HAS
    `the public have access to the building in order to view it or part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the public have access in order to view a collection or part of a collection housed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the collection is made or exhibited for the purpose of effecting sales or other commercial dealings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `removed from the building or its grounds the whole or part of an article` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the article was displayed or kept for display to the public in the building or that part of it or in its grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `removed it with lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the article was there as part of, or on loan for exhibition with, a collection intended for permanent exhibition to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
    `removed it on a day when the public have access to the building` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believed he had lawful authority for the removal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believed he would have lawful authority if the person entitled to give it knew of the removal and the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12.
DECLARE `Conveyance facts` HAS
    `constructed or adapted for the carriage of a person or persons by land, water or air` IS A BOOLEAN
    `constructed or adapted for use only under the control of a person not carried in or on it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a pedal cycle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is the subject of a hiring agreement or hire-purchase agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person in possession under the hiring or hire-purchase agreement consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he had other lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took it for his own or another's use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `drove it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `allowed himself to be carried in or on it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rode it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew it had been taken without such consent or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believed he had lawful authority to do what he did` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believed he would have the owner's consent if the owner knew of his doing it and the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Who prosecutes` IS ONE OF
    `a public prosecutor`
    `another person, after a public prosecution on the same facts was discontinued`
    `another person, in any other case`

-- s 12(4A) to (4C).
DECLARE `Time limit facts` HAS
    `the vehicle is mechanically propelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are of the kind described in section 12(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
    `who is prosecuting` IS A `Who prosecutes`
    `the date sufficient evidence to justify the proceedings came to the knowledge of the person section 12(4B) names` IS A DATE
    `the date the earlier public prosecution was discontinued` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Time limit position` IS ONE OF
    `section 12(4A) sets no limit on these proceedings`
    `section 12(4A) allows these proceedings to be commenced`
    `section 12(4A) bars these proceedings`

-- s 12(4).
DECLARE `Alternative verdict facts` HAS
    `tried on indictment for theft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the jury are not satisfied the accused committed theft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is proved the accused committed an offence under section 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12A(7) and (2)(a). Dangerous driving is defined by s 12A(7); "on a road or
-- other public place" is in s 12A(2)(a).
DECLARE `Dangerous driving facts` HAS
    `the vehicle was driven on a road or other public place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was driven in a way which falls far below what would be expected of a competent and careful driver` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it would be obvious to a competent and careful driver that driving in that way would be dangerous` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12A(1)(b), (3) and (8). One record for each of the circumstances (a) to (d)
-- of s 12A(2). The last two fields are the two defences in s 12A(3), which the
-- accused must prove.
DECLARE `Vehicle-taking circumstance` HAS
    `the driving, accident or damage happened` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by then the vehicle had been unlawfully taken` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by then the vehicle had been recovered, that is restored to its owner or to other lawful possession or custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it happened before he committed the basic offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he was neither in nor on nor in the immediate vicinity of the vehicle when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12A.
DECLARE `Aggravated vehicle-taking facts` HAS
    `the basic offence` IS A `Conveyance facts`
    `the vehicle he took is mechanically propelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dangerous driving` IS A `Dangerous driving facts`
    `circumstance (a), driving dangerously` IS A `Vehicle-taking circumstance`
    `circumstance (b), an accident owing to the driving injured a person` IS A `Vehicle-taking circumstance`
    `circumstance (c), an accident owing to the driving damaged property other than the vehicle` IS A `Vehicle-taking circumstance`
    `circumstance (d), damage was caused to the vehicle` IS A `Vehicle-taking circumstance`
    `the accident in circumstance (b) caused the death of the person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12A(5), (6).
DECLARE `Aggravated vehicle-taking alternative verdict facts` HAS
    `charged with an offence under section 12A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `found not guilty of the offence under section 12A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is proved he committed the basic offence` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 13.
DECLARE `Electricity facts` HAS
    `used electricity without due authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused electricity to be wasted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused electricity to be diverted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dishonest in dealing with the electricity` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 14(2) names the jurisdictions of the British postal area; s 36(3) uses the same list
-- for where the Act extends.
DECLARE `Jurisdiction` IS ONE OF
    `England and Wales`
    `Scotland`
    `Northern Ireland`
    `the Isle of Man`
    `the Channel Islands`
    `outside the British postal area`

-- s 14. The stealing in both limbs is the one in `the robbery`: when there was no
-- force, the robbery fields are simply false and only that stealing is read.
DECLARE `Mail facts` HAS
    `the robbery` IS A `Robbery facts`
    `attempted to steal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is a mail bag, a postal packet, or any of the contents of either` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was in the course of transmission as such` IS A BOOLEAN
    `transmitted from` IS A `Jurisdiction`
    `transmitted to` IS A `Jurisdiction`
    `in stealing or with intent to steal it, attempted robbery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `did it outside England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Section 34 - gain, loss and goods`

-- s 34(2)(a). "Gain" and "loss" extend only to gain or loss in money or other
-- property, temporary or permanent; "gain" includes keeping what one has, and "loss"
-- includes not getting what one might get. Only the first restriction removes
-- anything, so only it is a fact here.
DECLARE `Gain or loss facts` HAS
    `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he intended to cause loss to another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Sections 15 to 21 - false accounting, company officers, documents, blackmail`

-- s 17. "Dishonestly" here is not the s 2 test (s 1(3)): the person states it.
DECLARE `False accounting facts` HAS
    `dishonest in falsifying or using the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gain or loss in view in falsifying or using the accounts` IS A `Gain or loss facts`
    `the thing is an account, or a record or document made or required for an accounting purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `destroyed it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `defaced it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `concealed it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `falsified it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made or concurred in making an entry in it which is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `omitted or concurred in omitting a material particular from it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in furnishing information for any purpose, produced or made use of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to his knowledge it is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 18.
DECLARE `Company officer facts` HAS
    `the body corporate's offence` IS A `False accounting facts`
    `it is proved that the offence was committed with his consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he purported to act in such a capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members and the act was his as a member in connection with his functions of management` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 19.
DECLARE `False statement facts` HAS
    `he is an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association, or purports to act as one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the affairs of the body corporate or association are managed by its members and he is a member publishing in connection with his functions of management` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published or concurred in publishing a written statement or account` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to his knowledge the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he intended to deceive members about its affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he intended to deceive creditors about its affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he intended to deceive a person who has entered into a security for the benefit of the body corporate or association` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 20(3). A valuable security.
DECLARE `Document facts` HAS
    `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it evidences the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it evidences the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it evidences the satisfaction of an obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a will or other testamentary document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a government department` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 20.
DECLARE `Suppression facts` HAS
    `the document` IS A `Document facts`
    `dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gain or loss in view in destroying, defacing or concealing it` IS A `Gain or loss facts`
    `destroyed, defaced or concealed it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 21.
DECLARE `Blackmail facts` HAS
    `the gain or loss in view in making the demand` IS A `Gain or loss facts`
    `made a demand with menaces` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he believed he had reasonable grounds for making the demand` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the menaces relate to action to be taken by the person making the demand` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Sections 22 to 25 - stolen goods, wrongful credits, going equipped`

-- s 24. Where goods came from, in the words of ss 24(1), (2), (4) and 24A(8).
DECLARE `Origin of goods` IS ONE OF
    `the goods originally stolen, or parts of them`
    `goods representing stolen goods in the hands of the thief, as proceeds of a disposal or realisation`
    `goods representing stolen goods in the hands of a handler, as proceeds of a disposal or realisation`
    `goods obtained by blackmail`
    `goods obtained by fraud`
    `money dishonestly withdrawn from an account to which a wrongful credit was made`
    `goods of some other origin`

-- s 24. One lot of goods. The first three yes/no facts are about the stealing, or
-- the blackmail or fraud, from which the goods come.
DECLARE `Goods facts` HAS
    `where the goods came from` IS AN `Origin of goods`
    `they are land, or a thing forming part of land that has not been severed from it by stealing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stealing, or the blackmail, was an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stealing, or the blackmail, amounted to an offence where and when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the fraud amounted to an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the money, or the part of it asked about, derives from the wrongful credit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they have been restored to the person from whom they were stolen, or to other lawful possession or custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person and anyone claiming through him have otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution in respect of the theft` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 22. "Dishonestly" here is not the s 2 test: the person states it.
DECLARE `Handling facts` HAS
    `the goods` IS A `Goods facts`
    `it was done in the course of the stealing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he knew or believed the goods were stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dishonest in dealing with the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he received the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he undertook the retention, removal, disposal or realisation of the goods by or for the benefit of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he assisted in the retention, removal, disposal or realisation of the goods by or for the benefit of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he arranged to receive them, or to undertake or assist in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 23.
DECLARE `Reward advertisement facts` HAS
    `it is a public advertisement of a reward for the return of goods which have been stolen or lost` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it uses words to the effect that no questions will be asked` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it uses words to the effect that the person producing the goods will be safe from apprehension or inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it uses words to the effect that money paid for the purchase of the goods or advanced by way of loan on them will be repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he advertised the reward` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he printed the advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he published the advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 24A. A wrongful credit.
DECLARE `Wrongful credit facts` HAS
    `a credit of an amount of money has been made to an account` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit is of money in a currency other than sterling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the account is kept by him, or he has a right or interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the account is kept with a bank` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the account is kept with a business in the course of which money received by way of deposit is lent to others` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the account is kept with a business another activity of which is financed wholly or to a material extent out of the capital of or the interest on money received by way of deposit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the account is kept with an electronic money issuer within paragraphs (a) to (j) of the definition in regulation 2(1) of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the account was overdrawn before or after the credit was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit derives, at least in part, from theft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit derives, at least in part, from blackmail` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit derives, at least in part, from fraud contrary to section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit derives, at least in part, from stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he knows or believes that the credit is wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he failed to take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to secure that the credit is cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dishonest in failing to take those steps` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 25.
DECLARE `Going equipped facts` HAS
    `he was at his place of abode` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he had an article with him` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with a burglary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with a theft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with taking a conveyance without authority, an offence under section 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the article was made or adapted for use in committing a burglary or theft` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Sections 26 to 36 and Schedule 1 - procedure, spouses, interpretation, commencement`

-- s 26.
DECLARE `Search facts` HAS
    `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 27(1) and (2).
DECLARE `Joint handling facts` HAS
    `he is charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, at different times or at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `two or more persons are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the jury are satisfied that he handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 27(3).
DECLARE `Previous dealings evidence facts` HAS
    `he is being proceeded against for handling stolen goods and for no other offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `evidence has been given of his having, or arranging to have, the goods in his possession, or of his undertaking or assisting in, or arranging to undertake or assist in, their retention, removal, disposal or realisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is that he has had in his possession, or undertaken or assisted in the retention, removal, disposal or realisation of, stolen goods from another theft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of that other theft` IS A DATE
    `the date of the offence charged` IS A DATE
    `the evidence is that he has been convicted of theft or of handling stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of that conviction` IS A DATE
    `days of written notice given to him of the intention to prove the conviction` IS A NUMBER

-- s 27(4).
DECLARE `Statutory declaration facts` HAS
    `the proceedings are for the theft of anything in the course of transmission, or for handling stolen goods from such a theft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the declaration says that the declarant despatched or received or failed to receive goods or a postal packet, or that they were in a particular state or condition when despatched or received` IS A BOOLEAN
    `oral evidence to the like effect would have been admissible in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days before the hearing or trial that a copy of the declaration was given to the person charged` IS A NUMBER
    `the person charged gave the prosecutor written notice requiring the declarant to attend` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days before the hearing or trial that he gave that notice` IS A NUMBER
    `the court allowed further time in special circumstances and he gave the notice within it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 29(2): paragraph 11 of Schedule 1 to the Magistrates' Courts Act 1952, as this
-- Act substitutes it. That Act is not among the inputs.
DECLARE `Summary trial facts` HAS
    `the offence is an indictable offence under the Theft Act 1968` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is robbery, aggravated burglary, blackmail or assault with intent to rob` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a burglary comprising the commission of, or an intention to commit, an offence which is not included in that Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a burglary in a dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry to the dwelling, or to the part of it where the burglary was committed, or to any building or part of a building containing the dwelling, was obtained by force or deception or by the use of any tool, key or appliance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person in the dwelling was subjected to violence or the threat of violence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is handling stolen goods from an offence not committed in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 30(4) and (5).
DECLARE `Step against him` IS ONE OF
    `proceedings are instituted against him`
    `an arrest without warrant made by his wife, husband or civil partner`
    `a warrant of arrest issued on an information laid by his wife, husband or civil partner`
    `some other step`

DECLARE `Spouse proceedings facts` HAS
    `the step taken` IS A `Step against him`
    `the offence is stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property which at the time belonged to his wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to commit such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the step is taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he is charged with committing the offence jointly with his wife, husband or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by a judicial decree or order (wherever made) he and his wife or husband were at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an order (wherever made) is in force providing for the separation of him and his civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person bringing the proceedings is his wife or husband` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 31.
DECLARE `Civil proceedings facts` HAS
    `the proceedings are for the recovery or administration of any property, for the execution of any trust or for an account of any property or dealings with property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he would be excused from the question or the order only because answering or complying may incriminate him or his spouse or civil partner of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement or admission was made in answering a question put, or complying with an order made, in such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is offered in proceedings for an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is offered against him` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is offered against his spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they married or became civil partners after the statement or admission was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `property has been stolen or obtained by fraud or other wrongful means` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only thing said to affect the title is the conviction of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 32(1).
DECLARE `Abolished offence` IS ONE OF
    `larceny`
    `robbery at common law`
    `burglary at common law`
    `receiving stolen property`
    `obtaining property by threats`
    `extortion by colour of office or franchise`
    `false accounting by public officers`
    `concealment of treasure trove`
    `cheating`
    `an offence under an enactment mentioned in Part I of Schedule 3, to the extent it depends on a section or part of a section in column 3 of that Schedule`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Abolition facts` HAS
    `the old offence` IS AN `Abolished offence`
    `the last day on which any part of the offence was committed` IS A DATE
    `the cheating relates to the public revenue` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Schedule 1 paragraph 2.
DECLARE `Fish facts` HAS
    `he unlawfully took or destroyed fish, or attempted to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the fish were in water which is private property or in which there is a private right of fishery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `he has been convicted of that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing was with him at the time for use for taking or destroying fish` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other person is committing an offence under paragraph 2(1), or the person acting with reasonable cause suspects he is` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is one that would be liable to forfeiture on the other's conviction` IS A BOOLEAN

